(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[26 1 "// _ssl's SSL objects (queue 209): _SSLSocket over a socket or two MemoryBIOs, SSLSession and MemoryBIO."] [27 1 "//"] [28 1 "// The pipe adapter. Go's tls.Conn wants a net.Conn it may block on; OpenSSL's callers (ssl.py over a"] [29 1 "// non-blocking socket, asyncio's SSLProtocol over MemoryBIOs) want SSL_ERROR_WANT_READ and an operation"] [30 1 "// resumed by the next call. So each SSL object runs its tls.Conn in a goroutine of its own (the engine) over"] [31 1 "// an in-memory transport: the engine's Read takes what the Python side fed it and, when there is nothing,"] [32 1 "// tells the Python side it wants input and waits; its Write appends to the bytes to send. Control alternates"] [33 1 "// strictly (the Python thread waits on the engine's event with the GIL released, the engine waits on the"] [34 1 "// Python side's resume), so the engine touches no Python object and the transport's buffers have one owner at"] [35 1 "// a time. The Python side feeds the engine one TLS record at a time (its header, then its length), never"] [36 1 "// more, so after an unwrap the plain bytes behind close_notify stay in the socket as with OpenSSL. A callback"] [37 1 "// the engine needs (the SNI callback) runs on the Python thread with the GIL. Writes and close_notify, which"] [38 1 "// never wait for input, are made on the Python thread directly once the handshake is done (tls.Conn's write"] [39 1 "// side is independent of its read side)."] [62 1 "// sslEngine is the goroutine side: the tls.Conn and its transport's buffers."] [109 1 "// call runs f on the Python thread (from the engine)."] [130 1 "// pySSLSocket is an SSL object (PySSLSocket)."] [134 24 "// nil: over MemoryBIOs"] [162 1 "// sslVerifyError is a certificate verification failure: OpenSSL's code and message."] [170 1 "// ---- the session cache of one connection: the session given, the session received ----"] [185 2 "// the session's id: its state's digest, so a resumed session renewed by the server keeps it (OpenSSL keeps"] [186 2 "// the session id across a resumption)"] [203 1 "// ---- the configuration ----"] [242 1 "// serverConfig is GetConfigForClient: the SNI callback run on the Python thread (it may switch the socket's"] [243 1 "// context), the configuration made of the context then in force, ALPN without a protocol in common answered"] [244 1 "// with none (CPython's callback returns SSL_TLSEXT_ERR_NOACK; Go's server would refuse the handshake)."] [256 19 "// replaced since the handshake looked"] [301 1 "// verify is _ssl's verification (OpenSSL's X509_verify_cert with the context's store, then X509_check_host when"] [302 1 "// check_hostname): the codes of OpenSSL's x509_vfy.h."] [361 30 "// VERIFY_CRL_CHECK_LEAF (and _CHAIN, which checks the leaf too)"] [385 31 "// VERIFY_X509_STRICT: RFC 5280's AKI on a certificate not self-issued"] [404 1 "// sslCheckHost is X509_check_host / X509_check_ip_asc: 0 when the certificate names host, else 62 (or 64 for an"] [405 1 "// address). The subject's common name is looked at only without a DNS name and without"] [406 1 "// HOSTFLAG_NEVER_CHECK_SUBJECT; a wildcard only as the whole leftmost label, over one label, with at least two"] [407 1 "// labels after it."] [443 1 "// ---- errors ----"] [445 1 "// sslReasons are OpenSSL's reasons of the alerts a peer sends, by alert number."] [459 1 "// sslGoReasons are OpenSSL's reasons for Go's own handshake errors, by the start of their text."] [474 1 "// sslReasonText is ERR_reason_error_string's form of a reason: lower case, words apart."] [492 1 "// raiseErr is PySSL_SetError for an operation's Go error: the exception CPython's _ssl raises for what OpenSSL"] [493 1 "// would have reported."] [536 1 "// ---- the transport's two ends on the Python side ----"] [553 1 "// need is how much the record being fed still needs: its header's rest, then its body's."] [569 16 "// not a TLS record: the engine refuses its header"] [583 1 "// fill feeds the engine the next bytes of the current record: false when they are not there yet (a"] [584 1 "// non-blocking socket, an empty incoming BIO)."] [642 1 "// flush sends what the engine wrote: into the outgoing BIO, or to the socket (a non-blocking one's rest kept,"] [643 1 "// SSLWantWriteError)."] [700 1 "// step hands control to the engine, starting op (nil: resuming it), until it waits for input or is done; the"] [701 1 "// callbacks it asks for run here."] [722 1 "// drive runs an engine operation (resuming the one in flight first) to its end: OpenSSL's loop of SSL_do_handshake"] [723 1 "// or SSL_read with the socket's waits; SSLWantReadError when its input is not there yet."] [788 1 "// ---- the methods ----"] [893 27 "// the peer closed the transport: SSL_shutdown's second call gives up"] [908 1 "// ---- wrap ----"] [1023 1 "// ---- SSLSession ----"] [1034 1 "// ---- MemoryBIO ----"] [1201 21 "// SSL_get_client_ciphers is a server's"] [1294 30 "// OpenSSL's session of a connection that got no ticket (yet)"] [1305 2 "// SSLSession"] [1327 2 "// MemoryBIO"] [1377 1 "// ---- PKCS #8 encryption (PBES2 with PBKDF2, RFC 8018), which Go's x509 does not read ----"] [1475 1 "// sslTimeout is the TimeoutError of an operation past the socket's timeout (the handshake's message with"] [1476 1 "// ERRSTR's prefix, as _ssl.c has it)."] [1484 1 "// sslPBKDF2 is RFC 8018's PBKDF2 with HMAC over prf (crypto/pbkdf2's Key is generic, which goi's table does not"] [1485 1 "// call)."] [1511 1 "// sslDistrustedSPKI are the SHA-256 digests of the public keys _ssl refuses in any chain (Modules/_ssl/"] [1512 1 "// distrusted_spki.h, gh-160040: the compromised eMudhra intermediates)."] [1535 1 "// afterHandshake is what OpenSSL keeps of a finished handshake: the context's session statistics, and the"] [1536 1 "// anchor its by-hash lookup loaded from a capath directory, now in the store (get_ca_certs lists it)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[86 25] [189 39] [190